    {
      "tag": "main",
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "h1",
          "children": [
            "Query reasoning and relational algebra workbook"
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "children": [
            "Supports meetings 6–10. Use ",
            {
              "tag": "a",
              "attrs": {
                "href": "setup.sql"
              },
              "children": [
                "the shared fixture"
              ]
            },
            " and ",
            {
              "tag": "code",
              "children": [
                "SET search_path TO course32;"
              ]
            },
            ". Each meeting has its own task set; do not try to finish all five in one class."
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 6: joins and multiplicity"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "ol",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Produce (student_name,event_title) for every booking. Predict six rows."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "List every student with their booked event if any. Keep Eli, who has none. Predict seven rows."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Return every event and only its paid bookings. Compare a payment predicate in ON with one in WHERE. Explain why Graph disappears in the second version."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Join students and events without the bookings relation. Predict the cardinality and explain why DISTINCT cannot repair the missing relationship."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 7: aggregation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "ol",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "For every event, report total bookings, paid bookings, and paid revenue. Preserve Graph with zeros."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Explain COUNT(*) versus COUNT(b.student_id) after a left join."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Find events with at least two bookings using HAVING; classify paid revenue as zero, below 30, or at least 30 using CASE."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Add another one-to-many relation on paper and show how joining it before aggregation can double revenue. Repair with preaggregation."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 8: subqueries and sets"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "ol",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Find students with no bookings using NOT EXISTS."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Find students booked in both SQL and Design using INTERSECT, then using two EXISTS predicates."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Find students booked in every event in RequiredEvent; explain the double NOT EXISTS pattern."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Run ",
                {
                  "tag": "code",
                  "children": [
                    "SELECT id FROM students WHERE id NOT IN (SELECT student_id FROM booking_probe)"
                  ]
                },
                ". Explain the empty answer and repair it. Does NOT EXISTS have the same NULL behavior?"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 9: algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "children": [
            "Use S=students, E=events, B=bookings. Classical relational algebra uses sets."
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "ol",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Write selection and projection for titles of events with fee ≥20."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Write an algebra expression for names of students booked into SQL."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Express students without bookings using difference. Ensure the two operands have compatible attributes."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Express students in both required events using intersection or division."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Project event_id from B using SQL with and without DISTINCT; explain the relationship to algebraic projection."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "h2",
          "children": [
            "Meeting 10: equivalence workshop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "ol",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Push a fee predicate below an inner join and verify the same tuples."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "For ",
                {
                  "tag": "code",
                  "children": [
                    "E LEFT JOIN B"
                  ]
                },
                ", move ",
                {
                  "tag": "code",
                  "children": [
                    "B.paid = true"
                  ]
                },
                " from ON to WHERE. Use Graph as a counterexample to equivalence."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Express students with any booking using EXISTS (a semijoin) and a join. Explain why the latter needs duplicate elimination to return one row per student."
              ]
            },
            {
              "tag": "li",
              "children": [
                "Show why pushing a filter on aggregate revenue below GROUP BY is generally invalid. Distinguish it from a filter on the grouping key."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "\n",
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "strong",
              "children": [
                "Submit each meeting:"
              ]
            },
            " numbered answers, runnable SQL where applicable, predicted and actual rows, and one counterexample. ",
            {
              "tag": "strong",
              "children": [
                "Stretch:"
              ]
            },
            " explain the result of the “every required event” query when RequiredEvent is empty."
          ]
        },
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    "\n"
  ]
}
